In the end I merged #49604 which was *slightly* more efficient using `substr()` instead of `erase()`, as `erase()` calls `left()` + `substr()`:
```cpp
void String::erase(int p_pos, int p_chars) {
	*this = left(MAX(p_pos, 0)) + substr(p_pos + p_chars, length() - ((p_pos + p_chars)));
}
```

But both solutions were good and equivalent, thanks for your contribution!
